NOTICE — Third-party interatomic potential parameter files
===========================================================

The MEAM parameter files in this directory (and the copies under
surface/data/meam_lammps/meam_potentials/) reproduce interatomic potential
parameterizations published by third parties. They are provided here solely
to make the calculations of the accompanying paper reproducible. The original
authors retain all rights to these parameterizations; these files are
EXCLUDED from the MIT and CC-BY-4.0 licenses that apply to the rest of this
repository.

Provenance:

1. Sn.Ravelo1997.meam / library.Sn.Ravelo1997.meam
   Parameterization: R. Ravelo and M. Baskes, Phys. Rev. Lett. 79 (1997)
   2482-2485. The LAMMPS-format files were constructed by us by transcribing
   the published parameters as tabulated in J. R. Vella et al., Phys. Rev. B
   95 (2017) 064202 (Table I).

2. Sn.Etesami2018.meam / library.Sn.Etesami2018.meam
   Parameterization: S. A. Etesami, M. I. Baskes, M. Laradji, E. Asadi,
   Acta Mater. 161 (2018) 320-330 (pure-Sn part).

3. Sn.Ko2018.meam / library.Sn.Ko2018.meam
   Parameterization: W.-S. Ko, D.-H. Kim, Y.-J. Kwon, M. Lee, Metals 8
   (2018) 900. Files as distributed by the NIST Interatomic Potentials
   Repository, entry "2018--Ko-W-S--Sn"
   (https://www.ctcms.nist.gov/potentials/entry/2018--Ko-W-S--Sn/).

If you use these potentials, cite the original publications above.
